      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When you feel like memories don't matter because the world has moved on, it's a sign of how deeply immersive your grief has become, not a reflection of your true worth. Remembering that time is linear while your pain is persistent can help you process the feeling that you are just \"waiting.\" This separation from reality is a common symptom of severe depression, which means your feelings don't have to define your existence. Reaching out to a mental health professional can provide the safety and perspective you need to begin connecting with the \"you\" that still exists.",
      "source": "target",
